## CXX_STD: src/hank_egm2.cpp and src/hank_egm3.cpp use std::barrier (C++20).
## Without this line some toolchains fall back to C++17 and fail on <barrier>.
## Keep it FIRST: tools/hooks/pre-commit-cxx-std.sh and
## tests/testthat/test-build-config.R both police this declaration.
CXX_STD = CXX20
## -pthread: the HANK EGM kernels use std::thread UNCONDITIONALLY
## (hank_egm2.cpp Egm2Pool, hank_egm3.cpp Egm3Pool / hank_egm3_step_cpp). On
## glibc < 2.34 libstdc++ needs the flag at BOTH compile and link time; without
## it std::thread's constructor throws
##   "Enable multithreading to use std::thread: Operation not permitted"
## at RUN time, so the default (threaded) HANK path fails on older Linux even
## though the package compiled and installed cleanly. macOS/clang accepts
## -pthread as a no-op, so a local build proves nothing about this -- exactly
## the 0.9.1.1 CXX_STD lesson, one flag over.
##
## Deliberately NOT mirrored in src/Makevars.win: Rtools links winpthreads
## implicitly and -pthread is unnecessary there.
PKG_CXXFLAGS = -pthread
PKG_LIBS = -pthread $(LAPACK_LIBS) $(BLAS_LIBS) $(FLIBS)
